# =============================================================================
# BPUT Result Fetcher , environment variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# WHAT NEEDS WHAT
# SEO / sitemap / Open Graph   → needs NOTHING. robots.txt, sitemap.xml and
#                                  og-image.png are static files in `public/`
#                                  and are served automatically. No env vars.
# ---------------
# Public student flow (`/`)      → needs NOTHING. An empty `.env` boots the
#                                  homepage, search, PDF export, KaTeX, and
#                                  the trend/grade charts (they talk to BPUT
#                                  directly).
#
# Home "BPUT Results             → needs Supabase (server + client vars) so
# Intelligence" analytics        →   the `log_result_view` /
# section (below the fold on /)  →   `get_results_analytics` RPCs work.
#                                  Without them the section shows
#                                  "Analytics unavailable" but the rest of
#                                  the page keeps working.
#
# `/admin` surface               → needs Supabase (server + client vars) +
#                                  a Google OAuth client wired in the
#                                  Supabase dashboard + a row in
#                                  `public.user_roles` for your user.
#
# `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`    → only if you write server code that uses
#                                  `supabaseAdmin` (none of the current
#                                  routes do).
#
# On a managed platform these are auto-managed. For local dev outside a
# Cloud, either point at your own hosted Supabase project OR run
# `supabase start` locally , see README §"Running the analytics locally".
# =============================================================================


# --- Supabase (server side: server functions, SSR helpers, auth middleware) ---
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-id"
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-id.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-anon-publishable-key"

# --- Supabase (client side: shipped into the browser bundle by Vite) ---
# MUST match the values above (same project, same anon key). Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, so we need both sets.
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-id"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-id.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-anon-publishable-key"

# --- Supabase service role (server-only; privileged) --------------------------
# DO NOT prefix with VITE_ , this must never be shipped to the browser.
# Only needed if you add server code that uses the `supabaseAdmin` client
# (nothing in this repo currently does).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"

# =============================================================================
# Google OAuth (for `/admin` "Continue with Google")
# =============================================================================
# There are NO Google-specific env vars in this repo. The app calls Supabase's
# Google provider DIRECTLY via `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth`
# (see src/routes/auth.tsx) , no third-party OAuth broker, no `/~oauth/*` route.
# That means it works identically on localhost, Vercel/Netlify/Cloudflare, and
# any custom domain.
#
# Configure the credentials in:
#   1. Google Cloud Console → Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application)
#      - Authorized redirect URI:
#          https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   2. Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Google
#      - Paste the Client ID + Secret
#   3. Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration
#      - Site URL + Redirect URLs must include every `${origin}/auth/callback`
#        you sign in from (localhost, prod domain, preview domains).
#
# See README ("Google OAuth Setup") for full step-by-step instructions.
# =============================================================================